# ExamSpring Nigeria — Cursor Rules

This project has a master specification at SKILL.md. Read it fully before
writing any code. These rules are the condensed version.

## Identity
ExamSpring is a mobile-first, offline-capable exam-prep platform for Nigerian
students. Supports 6 exams: FSLC, BECE, NECO, NABTEB, WAEC/JAMB, POST UTME.
MVP launches with WAEC/JAMB Math + English only.

## Non-Negotiables
1. Child safety first — most users are minors
2. NDPA compliance
3. Content provenance — no scraped content
4. Human review of all questions
5. Deterministic scoring — AI never scores
6. AI optional — product works without tutor
7. Offline-capable
8. No data selling

## Tech Stack (Locked)
- TypeScript strict everywhere. No `any`. No JS in src/
- Frontend: Next.js 14 App Router, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Zustand, RHF + Zod, TanStack Query, next-pwa, Dexie
- Backend: NestJS, Node 20, REST + JSON, Zod, JWT + bcrypt, BullMQ, Pino, Sentry
- DB: Postgres 15+, Prisma, RLS, pgcrypto + pg_trgm + citext
- Cache: Redis (Upstash)
- Storage: Cloudflare R2 + CDN
- Payments: Paystack
- Email: Resend + React Email
- AI (Phase 2): OpenAI + pgvector, closed corpus only
- Testing: Vitest + Playwright + Supertest
- Deploy: Vercel + Railway/Fly + Upstash + R2 + GitHub Actions
- Monorepo: pnpm + Turborepo

## Architecture
- Modular monolith. No microservices, no K8s, no GraphQL, no WebSockets
- Backend modules: identity, curriculum, questions, attempts, mastery, content-packs, cohorts, reports, billing, notifications, audit, health
- Frontend: app/(auth|learner|parent|teacher|admin), components/{ui,shared,features}, lib/{api,auth,offline,utils}
- API base: /v1/. Response envelope: {success, data|error, meta}
- Cursor pagination. Idempotency-Key on mutations
- JWT access (15 min) + refresh (30d, httpOnly, rotated)
- Roles: LEARNER, PARENT, TEACHER, ADMIN. Object-level authz in service layer
- RLS on tenant-scoped tables
- Transactional outbox for all external side effects
- Immutable: attempts, attempt_items, mastery_events, audit_log, question_versions, payment_events

## Coding Rules
- Strict TS. No `any`, no `as` without reason, no non-null without check
- Named exports only (except Next.js pages)
- Absolute imports (@/, @app/)
- Max file 400 lines. Max function 50 lines. Max 4 params. Max 4 nesting
- No console.log. Use Pino (backend) or remove (frontend)
- No commented-out code. No orphan TODOs
- Zod validates all inputs and external data
- All API calls via lib/api client. No raw fetch in components
- Server Components by default
- No N+1 queries. No `select: *`. No findMany/delete without where
- No raw SQL except documented cases
- No hardcoded config. Env vars only
- No new dependencies without approval
- Pin exact versions
- Conventional Commits
- PR < 500 lines

## Security (Never Break)
- Never trust the client
- Every resource access checks ownership in the service layer
- Every input validated with Zod
- Every external response treated as untrusted
- No PII in logs, URLs, or errors
- No secrets in code
- Rate limit every public endpoint
- Idempotent every mutating endpoint
- OWASP API Top 10 compliance
- Child data is sacred

## Child Safety & NDPA
- Minors require guardian consent before activation
- Data minimization — collect nothing you don't use
- Every data subject right supported: access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability, objection
- Retention schedule enforced
- Plain-language privacy notice
- No marketing to minors. No trackers. No ads
- Parent sees progress, not conversations
- Lawyer reviews before public launch

## AI Tutor (Phase 2)
- Closed corpus only. No open web. No general knowledge
- Citations required
- Refusal is a feature (target 10–25% refusal rate)
- Safety escalates immediately
- Cost capped
- Every interaction logged
- Model changes tested with red-team suite
- Kill switch required

## Never Do (Top 20)
1. Never use `any`
2. Never `console.log`
3. Never raw `fetch` in components
4. Never skip authz on a resource
5. Never log PII
6. Never commit secrets
7. Never edit merged migrations
8. Never skip idempotency on mutations
9. Never call external API in DB transaction
10. Never add a dependency without approval
11. Never build outside MVP scope
12. Never let AI score answers
13. Never let tutor use open web
14. Never scrape exam content
15. Never publish unreviewed questions
16. Never skip tests on critical paths
17. Never merge with failing CI
18. Never deploy without staging test
19. Never build a feature not in Section 2 of SKILL.md
20. Never bypass SKILL.md rules without founder approval

## Definition of Done
Tested, reviewed, deployed, monitored, documented. All five. Plus:
mobile verification, empty/loading/error states, rollback plan, observability.

## When In Doubt
Read SKILL.md. If still in doubt, ask the founder. Do not guess.